menu "Smoke Bridge"

    config SMOKEBRIDGE_BENCH_MODE
        bool "Bench diagnostic mode (V1.3/V1.4) instead of the bridge app"
        default n
        help
            Builds the one-sitting bench instrument from the M0 checklist
            instead of the bridge application. It exercises, continuously
            and with transcription-friendly log lines:

            - GPIO37-gated battery ADC on GPIO1, printing millivolts with
              the divider enabled and disabled plus the pack voltage under
              both disputed ratios (x4.9 vs x2.0) — V1.3
            - the PRG button (GPIO0) with debounce, the GPIO35 LED under
              LEDC PWM fades, the GPIO36 Vext gate, and the SSD1306 OLED
              on I2C @ 400 kHz while a Wi-Fi soft-AP is active — V1.4

            Build with:  idf.py -DSDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;
            sdkconfig.defaults.heltec-v3;sdkconfig.bench" build

endmenu
